<p>It is a good article, but there are some glaring problems.</p>
<p>The Containment makes it clear and all-too-relevant that gravestones and coffins are transplanted from somewhere else to some other place, but the description gives nothing about it. Although the log does include a coffin it doesn't disappear either, so there is no relation whatsoever between the article and its containment procedures (apart from keeping people from entering).</p>
<p>Also it is said that the con artist evaded the Foundation in the past, but stops on that and it doesn't have any impact in the story whatsoever, so it must either be elaborated on or removed, IMHO, 'cause it does stand out.</p>
<p>Some info on the prices at the bar itself would be good, although it already made it clear that it costs actual common money. I would argue for a more thorough investigation on all the things, but it doesn't really need it.</p>

