														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4837690">
									

<p>I was summoned by PM. Let's do this!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Here,&nbsp;have&nbsp;some&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;OK,&nbsp;now&nbsp;give&nbsp;me&nbsp;back&nbsp;my&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>First of all, I want to clarify that humor is subjective (I laugh with almost everything), so I might not be able to tell if people will like this or not. I'll give you crit from my point of view.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A club classified as an SCP-J by the CKG Gathering due to its ability to erase memories</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I think this would be the second article regarding the CKG Gathering, so there's almost nothing about CKG's lore. You may or may not expand it, but you'll need to explain some things here: Why do the CKG want to erase memories? What's the object class? What are their &quot;protocols&quot; for the usage of the club?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>will subvert the reader's expectation by revealing the Foundation simply decided to use other tools to bash heads</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You can achieve this by constantly calling them &quot;amnestics&quot;, and then revealing a photo of an aluminium bat(And I think that would be really funny, ngl). But I'm concerned about the way you're going to write the article. Are you going to add interviews, reports, test logs&#8230;? Of course, they all would be in the 'CKG format', but I want to know what kind of layout you're going to use, especially to display the modern version of the object.</p>
<p>Also, while I like the idea of hitting someone in the head to erase their memory, I feel like this is a little&#8230; sour. I think you should add some kind of story to it, even a little one. Maybe they were using the same guy for all the tests and they had comedic reactions? Maybe some people used the object by accident? Maybe the CKG kept using it on each other by accident or something?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, I really like this idea, but humor is <em>very</em> subjective, so I'll suggest reaching out to other reviewers to see their opinions.</p>
<p>Feel free to contact a member of the <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a> to get more crit, or PM me to take another look!</p>

							</div>

								
					
