														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4837689">
									

<p>Honestly I hate discourse like this, since most of the trouble comes down to canon being a patchwork quilt, but I gotta disagree with your assessment of the Foundation. I think focusing on their methods and ignoring their substance does them a disservice.</p>
<p>Because like, I think prisons are bad? I think locking up people is bad and I'm not really interested in how jailers perceive themselves, they're still jailers. They may think they're doing necessary evils and all but at the bottom of their beliefs is (ostensibly) a desire to maintain the Veil and I couldn't disagree with them more.</p>
<p>But yeah, like, the versions the SH that are more obviously flawed in the ways you describe are pretty cool; I do wish they had more consistent characterization.</p>

							</div>

								
					
